yxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T04:04:37-07:00","id":1259379,"title":"","content":"Then... why? Why Mongolia? Why pick there as opposed to any other place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T04:18:28-07:00","id":1259382,"title":"","content":", partly because it has a low population density and it\u2019s easier to get away with supernatural Shenanigans. And partly becuase I\u2019m interested in Mongolian culture and history","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T04:30:20-07:00","id":1259385,"title":"","content":"Mongolia has a big tradition of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamanism_in_Siberia\" target=\"_blank\">local shamanistic believes</a>. In official <b>CoD</b> coverage, from what I remember, all the area of it are roots of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1255176-kindred-clans-lands-of-origin#post1255176\"><i>Mikhaili</i> vampire lost Clan</a>, Lodge Eaters of the Dead for werewolves ( hunting undead ) and <i>Ulgan</i> ephemera-based Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:36:30-08:00","id":1269053,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the book &quot;Red Shambhala&quot; by Andrei Znamenski. It's about the effort to create a Buddhist/Communist Utopia during the early 20th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T15:08:49-08:00","id":1269367,"title":"","content":"<b>The Eagle Huntress</b> (2016), a pretty good documentary about a 13 year old Kazakh girl involved in the Mongolian sport of eagle hunting (basically falconry with eagles).<br /> <br /> <b>A Pearl in the Forest</b> (2008), a drama about the Soviet purges in Mongolia during the 1930s.<br /> <br /> <b>Mongol</b> (2007), an epic biopic about Genghis Khan.<br /> <br /> Andrei Znamenski's <b>Red Shambhala</b>, a nonfiction look at the Soviet Union's attempts to manipulate and co-opt central and East Asian Buddhist and animist beliefs for their own political ends.<br /> <br /> Kevin Turner's <b>Sky Shamans of Mongolia</b>, a sort of travelogue among the country's modern practitioners, both rural and urban.<br /> <br /> Stephen Bodio's <b>Eagle Dreams</b>, an account of his travels in Mongolia right after the collapse of the Soviet Union in the 90s.<br /> <br /> Jack Weatherford's <b>The Secret History of the Mongol Queens</b>, about Genghis Khan's daughters, which is a followup to his earlier <b>Genghis Khan and the Making of the Modern World</b>.<br /> <br /> Carl Hoffman's <i>The Lunatic Express</i>, in which he travels the world using some of the most dangerous and bizarre methods possible, includes a section where he travels Western China and Mongolia. Tangentially is Paul Theroux's <i>Riding the Iron Rooster</i>, about traveling China, including the western regions and the boarders with Mongolia, by train.<br /> <br /> And the various travels guides about the country from groups like Lonely Planet, Culture Smart and Rough Guide. Also, PBS's<b> Roughing It: Mongolia </b>(2017).<br /> <br /> RPG-wise, the only stuff about Mongolia deal with the period of Genghis Khan's empire, with the Vampire: the Dark Ages sourcebook<i> Wind from the East: Mongols</i> and the Mythic Russia expansion <i>The Golden Horde</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T17:42:54-08:00","id":1273179,"title":"","content":"More inspiration than